From: Agent
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: sunxi: SPL: wait for DAT0 (card busy) before a data command

Samsung KLMAG2WEPD (stick2) froze the SoC shortly after init when data
commands were issued back to back; a 2 s idle after init made the whole FIT
read succeed. Do not start a data transfer while the card holds DAT0 low.
'B' is printed once if the card was ever seen busy.

---
 drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/sunxi_mmc.c
@@ -362,4 +362,18 @@
 	if (priv->fatal_err)
 		return -1;
+#ifdef CONFIG_XPL_BUILD
+	if (data) {
+		unsigned int busy_loops = 2000000;
+		int saw_busy = 0;
+
+		while ((readl(&priv->reg->status) & SUNXI_MMC_STATUS_CARD_DATA_BUSY) &&
+		       --busy_loops) {
+			if (!saw_busy) {
+				saw_busy = 1;
+				putc('B');
+			}
+		}
+	}
+#endif
 	if (cmd->resp_type & MMC_RSP_BUSY)
 		debug("mmc cmd %d check rsp busy\n", cmd->cmdidx);
